WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV — three-body (60s) Narrator Bill

1
00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.269
Unit tests pass in isolation while rockets, databases,

2
00:00:05.269 --> 00:00:10.056
and distributed clouds fail at the seams between teams.

3
00:00:11.289 --> 00:00:15.039
Each role holds private mental models about units,

4
00:00:15.039 --> 00:00:19.915
failure modes, and ordering that never make it into source types.

5
00:00:21.148 --> 00:00:25.693
A repair stays fixed if and only if every assumption

6
00:00:25.693 --> 00:00:31.811
crossing a module or role handoff is stated and mechanically verified.

7
00:00:33.044 --> 00:00:39.471
Csmith fuzzing found bugs in every compiler except CompCert's verified middle-end,

8
00:00:39.471 --> 00:00:43.390
pinpointing remaining risk to unchecked frontends.

9
00:00:44.623 --> 00:00:48.570
Because AI agents lack unwritten human context,

10
00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:54.616
making software safe for agents resolves computing's three-body problem.
